          "path": "_m/g/c/6/f/knocktopher-wp/knocktopher-abbey-co-kilkenny-.jpg",
          "filename": "Knocktopher Abbey, Co. Kilkenny - geograph.org.uk - 206338.jpg",
          "caption": "Knocktopher Abbey, Co. Kilkenny. Parts of a Norman Castle and a 13C abbey are incorporated into a neo-Gothic house of 1850, now a time-share resort.  The chimney to the left of the dormer windows is said to be 500 years old and the oldest chimney in Ireland still in use.  On the left is one of the mews cottages.",
